      "title": "Log query recipes",
      "description": "The queries an operator needs during an incident, so they do not have to remember LogQL.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 11, "w": 10, "x": 14, "y": 56 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Follow one journey end to end\n\nEvery record carries `requestId`; the worker's carry `correlationId` too. Both are **log fields, never labels** — that is deliberate, and it is why they are queried with `|=` rather than selected with `{}`.\n\n```logql\n{namespace=~\"embroidery.*\"} |= \"<requestId>\"\n```\n\n### One failing checkout\n\n```logql\n{namespace=~\"embroidery.*\", app=\"api\"}\n  | json\n  | event = \"http.request.completed\"\n  | http_route = \"/api/public/ready-made-orders\"\n  | http_statusCode >= 500\n```\n\n### Unhandled API faults\n\n```logql\n{namespace=~\"embroidery.*\", app=\"api\", level=\"error\"}\n  | json | event = \"platform.error\"\n```\n\n### One job kind in the worker\n\n```logql\n{namespace=~\"embroidery.*\", app=\"worker\"}\n  | json | jobKind = \"NOTIFICATION_DELIVERY\"\n```\n\n### Storefront and Admin server errors\n\n```logql\n{namespace=~\"embroidery.*\", app=~\"storefront|admin\", level=\"error\"}\n```\n\n---\n\n**What you will not find in a log line.** Secure tokens, verification and step-up codes, cookies, `Authorization` values, customer contact details and raw evidence payloads are redacted at the source by the `APP12-H01` policy. If you need to identify a customer, take the `requestId` to the Admin surface — not to the logs."
      }
    }
